 #:seon.task{:name "a-repl-test-after-a-root-ns-form-has-no-executable-var"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Root evaluated on main the file's (ns seon.ref-test ...) with two added requires, then the deftest seon.ref-test/a-resolved-function-offers-a-source-form-that-shows-its-source (fanout-2 run, default 795a770c2, 2026-10-08). Called at root's or the agent's REPL it runs, but every test-world run of it, on main and on agent fan2-source's branch after a correct fix, records error 1 with began? false and the failure \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", so its task can never go green. Deftests defined the same way in seon.db-test and seon.transact-feedback-test without an ns form run and fail on their assertions. Without an ns form it happens too when the body names the test file's private helpers or aliases (fanout-3, default 324461975, 2026-10-09: root's seon.help-test/help-teaches-how-a-deftest-names-its-task over with-help-agent, taught-forms and the bootstrap alias recorded the same error; the same deftest with only fully qualified calls ran and failed on its assertion), because root's SCI context has not loaded the test namespace. Done when a deftest root defines at its REPL after an ns form runs in the test world as at the REPL."
             :must-read #{seon.test/resolve-test seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-proof-that-evaluates-agent-code-reuses-its-red"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Since `f5e4ec35d` (F11, an unchanged red answered from its record) a task proof that reaches the agent's definitions only through evaluated code, as every `seon.competency-test` proof does through `seon.test-support/agent-value`, keeps its first red: its reach digest does not change when the agent defines `comp.geo/area`, so the step answers the old red and the task never goes green. `seon.competency-grade-test/a-fixture-model-run-grades-green` passes at `100f08747` (`bin/seon check --at 100f08747`, run 1078ca606457) and fails at `f5e4ec35d` (run da39358e68af: proofs {:red 1} after the correct model reply), as does `seon.competency-grade-test/a-launch-grades-each-run`. Done when a task's proofs run again after any eval request that changed the branch's program, while unrelated unchanged reds stay answered from their record."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.turn/run-proofs seon.test-support/agent-value}}
 #:seon.task{:name "destructive-reach-keeps-a-second-cache"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.test/destructive-reach memoizes its walk in a clojure.core.cache LRU (threshold 4) held in the schema projection's cache value, beside seon.cache: a second cache with its own bound and no recordStats, which AGENTS.md refuses. Done when the walk is a seon.cache kind keyed by the same content key and clojure.core.cache.wrapped is no longer required by seon.test."
             :must-read #{seon.test/destructive-reach seon.cache/lookup}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-malformed-task-tag-stops-the-whole-check"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A malformed `:seon/tasks` value on one deftest stopped a whole `bin/seon check` with an exception (lane h1-prose, 2026-10-09) instead of returning an error on that one test beside the others' results (AGENTS.md: nothing crashes; errors are data)."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run}}]
